## Computer Network vs IT?
		· Computer Network - allows digital communication between computers (nodes) to share resources and exchange data.
		· All of IT (Information Technology) - revolves around transferring information through connected systems.
## Common Networking Orgs?
		· IEEE, IANA, IETF, ICANN, ITU, TIA
  IEEE – networking and technology standards
  IETF – Internet standards and protocols. Governs TCP/IP layers 2-7. 
  IANA – Internet number and protocol registries
  ICANN – coordinates domain names and Internet identifiers
  ITU – international telecommunications standards and coordination
  TIA – telecommunications and ICT standards
## Components of Computer Networking
		1. Physical Components – cables, switches, routers, network cards, access points, etc. 
		2. Network Configuration – IP address, subnet mask, gateway, DNS, DHCP, and other network settings. 
		3. Network Types – LAN, WAN, MAN, PAN. 
		4. Network Protocols – TCP/IP, HTTP/HTTPS, DNS, DHCP, FTP, etc. 
Transmission Methods – Ethernet, Wi-Fi, fiber optic, Bluetooth, cellular, etc.
